<<<
+ confined to the merely defining sense * of the (Greek) Sophists ’. Sophy, -ie. See -EY, -IE, -y. soprano. Pl. -os, see -o(£)s 6, or -ni (-é). sorceress. See FEMININE DESIG- NATIONS. sore, adv. For s. afflicted, let & hindered, &c., see UNIDIOMATIC -LY. sorites(sori’téz). TECHNICALTERMS. sorrow. For ‘ more in s. than in anger’, & ‘in her &c. great s.’, see HACKNEYED PHRASES, & STOCK PATHOS.
===
+ confined to the merely defining sense ‘of the (Greek) Sophists’.

**Sophy, -ie.** See ^^-EY^^, ^^-IE^^, ^^-Y^^.

**soprano.** Pl. *-os*, see ^^-O(E)S^^ 6, or *-ni* (-ē).

**sorceress.** See ^^FEMININE DESIGNATIONS^^.

**sore,** adv. For *s. afflicted, let & hindered,* &c., see ^^UNIDIOMATIC -LY^^.

**sorites** (sorī'tēz). ^^TECHNICAL TERMS^^.

**sorrow.** For ‘more in s. than in anger’, & ‘in her &c. great s.’, see ^^HACKNEYED PHRASES^^, & ^^STOCK PATHOS^^.
>>>

